cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this manuscript or code in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Finite-Bar Discrete General Relativity: Lattice Waves on a Planck-Density (Hayward) Black Hole"
abstract: "Scalar test field on a Planck-spaced cubic lattice propagating on a fixed Painleve-Gullstrand / Hayward regular black-hole background, with 18- and 27-point isotropic stencils, a skew-symmetric summation-by-parts Killing Hamiltonian, Cayley symplectic evolution, and a phenomenological local saturation rule. Includes a verification suite with a claims audit: GR is recovered outside the horizon by construction; the inner Cauchy horizon remains; local saturation moves inner-horizon blueshift into core mass rather than removing it; which interior completion the lattice rule selects remains open."
